      "message": "fix(post): cap a feed that turns a rotary at the machine's stated rates\n\nOne prelude rule (post::rotary_cap: rotaryRate / rotaryFeedCap /\nrotaryFeed / rotaryFeedWord) caps the F of every feed block that turns a\nrotary so no rotary runs past its stated deg/min and no linear part past\nthe fastest stated feed, read the way each control reads F:\n\n- fanuc.cps and doosan-dnm.cps under G43.4: F is the tool tip's speed,\n  the rotaries carried along (F <= rate * tip / |d|; tip still: F <= rate).\n- doosan-dnm.cps on a 4th axis without TCP and fanuc-lathe.cps C-axis\n  live tooling: one composite length, degrees counted as mm.\n  fanuc-lathe.cps now calls the shared rule instead of its own copy.\n- Arcs that turn a rotary: the path rule over the chord in the arc's\n  plane (never looser than any reading of an arc's F).\n\nA capped F is floored to 0.1 mm/min. A feed that turns a rotary from an\nangle the post never wrote is refused by name when that rotary states a\nrate; each such refusal counts once per program. Unstated rates cap\nnothing, so every golden posts byte-identical text. tormach.cps writes A\nonly on a G0 index and needs no cap.\n\nfourth_axis_pose's tilted fixture now opens with a rapid that places the\nrotary (its feeds would otherwise turn A from an unknown angle).\n\nFixes #885\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAgjpiZbXSvmXLvdmL",
